{"kind":"assert","text":"Clarification for cards request a9551a6d, after the planner's 17 October review of the views design against the MCP Apps specification (stable 2026-01-26 and draft), both chat hosts' published design guidelines, the 25 official ext-apps examples and 45 vendor-style examples. Every existing condition stays. Four conditions are added to the revision and the S2 kit, and one line goes to S0.\n\n1. Generic kit, lane views as instances. The kit's card takes an item kind, the displayed revision, the actor chip, the reasons this item needs this person, at most two acts bound to the displayed revision, a one-line model context, and a text fallback. Needs you, Work, Decision and Change are composed from that card. The kit itself knows nothing about lanes.\n\n2. Model context contract. Every card tells the model what it shows through ui/update-model-context: the item, its revision, the entry positions read, who it waits on, and what settles it. S2 witness: the context names the exact displayed revision, and an act the model then makes on that card binds to that revision.\n\n3. Host rules. Host style variables for structure, with brand colour on accents only; no custom fonts; no wordmark where the host already shows the app name; inline shows a summary and fullscreen shows the detail, with Back closing fullscreen; superseded card instances are disabled; free text goes to the composer, not to a field in the card; \"actions that suit each screen\" means at most two per card; every view tool returns a useful text result for hosts without views.\n\n4. Receipts. After an act the card advances in place and records the receipt in model context with a short text line. A chat message through ui/message is sent only when the person hands off to the model. Browser checks in S2 compare this with the prototype's message-per-act loop, and the revision records which one the rehearsal keeps and why.\n\nS0 addition: the sandbox domain is inguz.space, registered in the Cloudflare account beside the existing deployments, with proxied apex and wildcard records. _meta.ui.domain and a later dap web host use \u003cid\u003e.inguz.space as the per-application sandbox origin. The kit reads each resource's content security policy from the package's resource metadata rather than a hard-coded empty policy; the journey's views still declare none.\n\nSequencing is unchanged: revision, checker review, planner read, then the kit. Voice, visual surfaces, media custody, the dap web host and the notice side channel are out of scope and will be filed after the journey's exit test."}